Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["Euclidean Infrageometry", "GuideTitle",
 CellID->942062912,ExpressionUUID->"a3a3c038-ca24-47b7-9945-83f1c1312fe3"],

Cell["\<\
Synthetic geometry of Euclidean-like objects in graphs. We provide a language \
for elementary multi-valued geometry at the infra-scale, and tools to study \
its convergence to the classical idealized \"infinitesimal\" Euclidean \
geometry, with \"breathless lines\", unique intersections, etc. We use inert \
atomic tokens to represent synthetic objects that can be used for symbolic \
work whose evaluation in a concrete graph is postponed.\
\>", "GuideAbstract",
 CellID->2001916300,ExpressionUUID->"ef0ab37b-2e0d-4399-8f7e-82603ccbe925"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["", "GuideFunctionsSection",
 CellID->1866139230,ExpressionUUID->"a0ea3657-4c83-4862-93c8-ecf80cebc774"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Basic Euclidean Synthetic Objects", "GuideFunctionsSubsection",ExpressionUUID->"0a4796e7-91b0-4c53-a6aa-0c633c2dbf96"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraSegment"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraSegment", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineGuideFunction",
  TaggingRules->{"PageType" -> "Function"},ExpressionUUID->
  "9fad021f-ef38-469e-a7f8-25b05e04e59f"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "the inert segment from p to q, every geodesic between them at once; with \
more points, the polyline of their consecutive segments"
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"f87158c7-ec37-4b2b-9f03-5ea66c694c20"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraRay"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraRay", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineGuideFunction",
  TaggingRules->{"PageType" -> "Function"},ExpressionUUID->
  "104f5a9f-28ed-46f7-b54a-2f0ba317b01c"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "the inert ray from p through q: the geodesics from p through q that no \
neighbour of their last vertex prolongs; InfraRay[p, p] is the pencil at p"
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"98935ce3-e47b-42a3-b803-bd409b58316b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraLine"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraLine", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineGuideFunction",
  TaggingRules->{"PageType" -> "Function"},ExpressionUUID->
  "c7a0e992-447d-446b-8769-d2ec79e72990"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "the inert line through p and q: the geodesics through both that no \
neighbour of either endpoint prolongs"
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"f57f0606-f033-4ce3-8217-852c382f6533"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraArc"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraArc", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineGuideFunction",
  TaggingRules->{"PageType" -> "Function"},ExpressionUUID->
  "d39cbb8a-f8f7-4253-82d6-d1d5ef2ad402"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "the inert arc around c from p1 to pk through the intermediate points: the \
geodesics of the band graph of the circle through p1"
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"47671a20-939f-4095-9ec9-3e9d712bf98b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraCircle"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraCircle", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineGuideFunction",
  TaggingRules->{"PageType" -> "Function"},ExpressionUUID->
  "c9ab54d5-2633-4a28-bd00-0566bcab15f4"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "the inert circle around c through p: the shortest cycles through p that \
separate c from the outside of its band; \"Radius\" -> r or {r, s} in place \
of p takes the whole band"
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"385cfdbd-4719-4e34-96f0-329a5bf641b5"],

Cell["\<\
waits: InfraEquidistantSet, the points at the same distance from the given \
points, {v : d(p1, v) == \[Ellipsis] == d(pn, v)}\
\>", "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"c00a141e-cbb5-4faf-bc2f-37496a560ccc"],

Cell["\<\
waits: InfraMidpoint, the center of the interval graph of p and q\
\>", "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"f067fcc7-ffad-4b9f-b6f4-55fa5575fcea"],

Cell["\<\
waits: InfraQuadric, its name and what it should be; today FindInfraQuadric \
gives the solid interior {v : d(p1, v) + \[Ellipsis] + d(pk, v) <= c}\
\>", "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"2bfa90e8-6fb9-480f-a47a-777bb04064b0"],

Cell["\<\
waits: InfraBallHull, the intersection of all balls of radius r that contain \
a set of points\
\>", "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"fbefecc4-d20d-4602-bd9e-be056a1b6405"],

Cell["\<\
waits: InfraConvexHull, the k-th layer of a filtration: layer 0 is the set, \
each next layer the union of all shortest paths between points of the one \
before\
\>", "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"f3ba0380-0eb8-4b8f-88b1-e9b2d8feb045"],

Cell["\<\
waits: InfraSphere, the separating connected subsets of the shell of radius r \
about a centre\
\>", "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"53ee421d-c3ff-4eff-9058-795a6aac3f57"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraBall"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraBall", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineGuideFunction",
  TaggingRules->{"PageType" -> "Function"},ExpressionUUID->
  "c821a855-2035-488d-a0a3-3069e16eba27"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "the closed ball {v : d(c, v) <= r} of radius r about c; today a scene token \
only"
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"522b3fef-41b9-4db0-8cc1-df3bff80c666"],

Cell["waits: InfraTube, the tube of radius s about a core", "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"69775c24-539b-4afe-9e2c-5bf3974eb9de"],

Cell["\<\
waits: InfraCone, the cone of a given slope with apex at one end of an axis\
\>", "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"f00fd2df-459a-4ba0-88ad-338f35fcdcbd"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraAngle"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraAngle", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineGuideFunction",
  TaggingRules->{"PageType" -> "Function"},ExpressionUUID->
  "83fdb0e7-d3d8-4b12-ba7a-40cff6136650"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "the angle at p between q1 and q2 in radians, Method \"Arclength\" or \
\"Alexandrov\", the comparison angle of the three distances; a method from \
the shortest paths waits"
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"3f836248-6392-4b28-bc0c-27ab804fad13"],

Cell["\<\
waits: InfraCrossection, an invariant of four points, as the distance is of \
two points and the angle of three\
\>", "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"c0570c79-5f0e-4dc1-8425-b9202009639d"]
}, Open  ]],

